{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.BridgeADeligneGauge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.BridgeADeligneGauge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.Derivation.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Action.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Mul","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Defs"],"declarations":27,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BridgeADeligneGauge.trivialAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BridgeADeligneGauge.trivialAction","kind":"def","line":316,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BridgeADeligneGauge.lean#L316-L324","doc":"The trivial deck group acting trivially. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BridgeADeligneGauge.intertwine_of_closure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BridgeADeligneGauge.intertwine_of_closure","kind":"theorem","line":277,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BridgeADeligneGauge.lean#L277-L304","doc":"Intertwining the monodromies on a generating set of the deck group suffices. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BridgeADeligneGauge.monodromy_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BridgeADeligneGauge.monodromy_one","kind":"theorem","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BridgeADeligneGauge.lean#L257-L267","doc":"The monodromy of the identity is the identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BridgeADeligneGauge.monodromy_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BridgeADeligneGauge.monodromy_mul","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BridgeADeligneGauge.lean#L241-L254","doc":"The monodromy of a fundamental solution is multiplicative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BridgeADeligneGauge.gauge_of_conj_monodromy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BridgeADeligneGauge.gauge_of_conj_monodromy","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BridgeADeligneGauge.lean#L187-L237","doc":"**Route B of Bridge A.**  Conjugate monodromy plus Deligne full faithfulness (both directions)\ngives an algebraic gauge transformation `g ∈ GL_N(R)` with `∂g = ω₂ g − g ω₁`, i.e.\n`ω₂ = (∂g + g ω₁) g⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BridgeADeligneGauge.intertwiner_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BridgeADeligneGauge.intertwiner_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BridgeADeligneGauge.lean#L166-L184","doc":"`h` is deck-invariant (single-valued) exactly when `C` intertwines the monodromies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BridgeADeligneGauge.intertwiner_horiz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BridgeADeligneGauge.intertwiner_horiz","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BridgeADeligneGauge.lean#L153-L162","doc":"`h = Φ₂ C Φ₁⁻¹` is horizontal for `Hom(∇₁, ∇₂)`, for any constant `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BridgeADeligneGauge.cst_der","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BridgeADeligneGauge.cst_der","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BridgeADeligneGauge.lean#L150-L151","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BridgeADeligneGauge.intertwiner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BridgeADeligneGauge.intertwiner","kind":"def","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BridgeADeligneGauge.lean#L141-L144","doc":"The candidate intertwiner `h = Φ₂ C Φ₁⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BridgeADeligneGauge.deck_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BridgeADeligneGauge.deck_inv","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BridgeADeligneGauge.lean#L135-L139","doc":"The deck action on `Φ⁻¹`: `γ • Φ⁻¹ = M(γ)⁻¹ Φ⁻¹`, written without inverting `M`:\n`Φ · M(γ) · (γ • Φ⁻¹) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BridgeADeligneGauge.horiz_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BridgeADeligneGauge.horiz_inv","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BridgeADeligneGauge.lean#L124-L133","doc":"The inverse of a fundamental solution satisfies `∂Φ⁻¹ = −Φ⁻¹ ω`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BridgeADeligneGauge.DeligneFullyFaithful","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BridgeADeligneGauge.DeligneFullyFaithful","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/BridgeADeligneGauge.lean#L115-L120","doc":"**Deligne full faithfulness** (the isolated analytic input): a single-valued horizontal\nsection of `Hom(∇₁, ∇₂)` is algebraic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.BridgeADeligneGauge.FundamentalSolution.deck","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.BridgeADeligneGauge.FundamentalSolution.deck","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"